# UDSM Connected Intelligent System - Staff and Alumni Mobile UI Code Description

## Project Summary

This Flutter project implements a mobile interface for the UDSM Connected Intelligent System. The current build supports Staff and Alumni UI flows from the same welcome screen. Student and Admin buttons are still shown as future roles, but they are intentionally disabled for now.

The app targets Android and iOS only. The Flutter web target was removed because the requested product is a mobile app, not a website. The UI is based on the PowerPoint prototype style: blue headers, UDSM branding, light grey page background, rounded white cards, small icon buttons, and bottom navigation. Staff screens keep the existing staff dashboard style, while Alumni screens add a separate alumni-focused shell, dashboard, feeds, networking, jobs, mentorship, profile, emergency, map, AI assistant, and feedback flows.

## Current User Flow

1. The app opens on a role-choice welcome screen.
2. The user can tap `Login as Staff` or `Login as Alumni`.
3. Staff login opens the existing staff login screen, then the staff home dashboard.
4. Staff users can move between Home, Alerts, Services, Calendar, AI, and Map using the staff bottom navigation.
5. Staff logout is now placed inside the staff Profile screen, opened from the Profile shortcut on the staff dashboard.
6. Alumni login opens the alumni SSO login screen.
7. Alumni users can also open Alumni Registration, then Registration Pending, then Account Approved screens.
8. After Alumni login, the Alumni dashboard opens and shows an automatic session timeout warning modal.
9. Alumni users can move between Home, Updates, Events, Jobs, and Profile using the alumni bottom navigation.
10. Alumni users can open the AI Assistant from the floating chatbot button placed above the bottom navigation bar.
11. Logout returns the app to the role-choice welcome screen.

This flow is currently simulated in local widget state. There is no backend authentication yet.

## Platform Setup

The project keeps these mobile platform folders:

- `android/`: Android native project files.
- `ios/`: iOS native project files.

The `web/` folder was removed. This means the app should be run on Android or iOS targets:

```sh
flutter run -d android
flutter run -d ios
```

## Assets

The app uses this asset:

- `assets/images/udsm_logo.png`

This image is the UDSM crest used on the welcome screen. It is registered in `pubspec.yaml`:

```yaml
flutter:
  uses-material-design: true
  assets:
    - assets/images/udsm_logo.png
```

Without this registration, `Image.asset('assets/images/udsm_logo.png')` would fail at runtime.

## `lib/main.dart`

This file is the app entry point.

### Imports

```dart
import 'package:flutter/material.dart';

import 'screens.dart';
import 'theme.dart';
```

- `material.dart` provides Flutter Material widgets such as `MaterialApp`.
- `screens.dart` contains the app UI screens and widgets.
- `theme.dart` contains the UCIS color palette and Material theme.

### `main()`

```dart
void main() {
  runApp(const UcisAdminApp());
}
```

`main()` is the first function Flutter runs. It starts the app by mounting `UcisAdminApp`.

### `UcisAdminApp`

`UcisAdminApp` is a `StatelessWidget` because the app-level wrapper does not hold mutable state. It returns a `MaterialApp`.

Important properties:

- `title: 'UDSM Mobile Application'`: app title used by the platform.
- `debugShowCheckedModeBanner: false`: removes the red debug banner.
- `theme: buildUcisTheme()`: applies the custom UCIS theme from `theme.dart`.
- `home: const UcisMobilePrototype()`: sets the first rendered widget to the mobile prototype in `screens.dart`.

## `lib/theme.dart`

This file defines the visual design system.

### Color Constants

The app uses named color constants so the same colors can be reused everywhere:

- `ucisBlue`: main brand blue used in headers, primary buttons, active navigation, and icons.
- `ucisBlueDark`: darker blue reserved for deeper brand states.
- `ucisInk`: dark text color.
- `ucisMuted`: secondary text color.
- `ucisLine`: border color for cards and inputs.
- `ucisCanvas`: page background color.
- `ucisGold`: warning/medium-priority accent.
- `ucisGreen`: success/connected/normal accent.
- `ucisRed`: error/high-priority/logout accent.

### `buildUcisTheme()`

This function returns a `ThemeData` object for the entire app.

It builds a `ColorScheme` using `ColorScheme.fromSeed`, with:

- `primary: ucisBlue`
- `secondary: ucisGold`
- `tertiary: ucisGreen`
- `error: ucisRed`
- `surface: Colors.white`
- `brightness: Brightness.light`

The returned `ThemeData` sets:

- `useMaterial3: true`: enables Material 3 styling.
- `scaffoldBackgroundColor: ucisCanvas`: default background.
- `fontFamily: 'Roboto'`: app font.
- `textTheme`: consistent headline, title, body, and label styles.
- `inputDecorationTheme`: rounded white text fields with grey borders and blue focus borders.
- `filledButtonTheme`: blue filled buttons with white text and rounded corners.
- `outlinedButtonTheme`: white/outlined buttons with dark text and rounded corners.

This keeps the visual style consistent without repeating button and input styling on every screen.

## `lib/screens.dart`

This is the main UI file. It contains both the app flow and all screen widgets.

### Top-Level App State: `UcisMobilePrototype`

`UcisMobilePrototype` is a `StatefulWidget` because it controls which screen is currently visible.

Its state class `_UcisMobilePrototypeState` stores:

```dart
int _page = -2;
```

The `_page` value acts as a simple navigation state machine:

- `-2`: role-choice welcome screen.
- `-1`: staff login screen.
- `0`: staff home dashboard.
- `1`: announcements screen.
- `2`: services screen.
- `3`: calendar screen.
- `4`: AI assistant screen.
- `5`: campus map screen.

Helper methods update this state:

- `_openStaffLogin()` sets `_page` to `-1`.
- `_openStaffHome()` sets `_page` to `0`.
- `_logout()` sets `_page` to `-2`.

Each method calls `setState`, which tells Flutter to rebuild the UI with the new screen.

### `build()` in `_UcisMobilePrototypeState`

The `build` method decides which screen to show:

- If `_page == -2`, show `WelcomeScreen`.
- If `_page == -1`, show `StaffLoginScreen`.
- Otherwise, show `PhoneShell` containing one of the signed-in staff pages.

The signed-in page is selected using a Dart `switch` expression:

- `0 => StaffHomeScreen`
- `1 => AnnouncementsScreen`
- `2 => ServicesScreen`
- `3 => CalendarScreen`
- `4 => AiAssistantScreen`
- `5 => CampusMapScreen`
- default returns `StaffHomeScreen`

The root widget is:

```dart
Scaffold(
  backgroundColor: ucisCanvas,
  body: SafeArea(child: phone),
)
```

`SafeArea` prevents the UI from going under the device notch, status bar, or system gesture areas. There is no external phone mockup frame anymore, so the app fills the actual device screen.

## Authentication and Role Screens

### `WelcomeScreen`

`WelcomeScreen` is the first screen. It receives:

```dart
final VoidCallback onStaffLogin;
```

This callback is called when the user taps `Login as Staff`.

The screen has two main parts:

1. A blue branded header.
2. A white rounded login-choice card.

The header includes:

- `UdsLogo`
- `UDSM MOBILE APPLICATION`
- `University of Dar es Salaam`
- `Connected Intelligent System`

The card includes:

- Title: `Welcome`
- Instruction text: `Choose your account type to continue.`
- Active button: `Login as Staff`
- Active button: `Login as Alumni`
- Disabled button: `Login as Student`
- Helper text: `Student access is disabled in this build. Staff and Alumni UI are available.`
- Disabled button: `Login as Admin`

Student and Admin buttons use `onPressed: null`, which makes Flutter render them as disabled.

### `StaffLoginScreen`

`StaffLoginScreen` is the staff sign-in form. It receives:

```dart
final VoidCallback onSignIn;
```

This callback opens the staff dashboard.

The screen uses:

- `UcisHeader` with title `Staff Login`.
- A `UcisCard` containing the form.
- A text field for staff email or ID.
- A password text field with `obscureText: true`.
- Helper text explaining staff access.
- A `Continue` button.

This is currently a prototype screen, so it does not validate credentials. Tapping `Continue` simulates successful login.

## Signed-In Layout

### `PhoneShell`

`PhoneShell` wraps all signed-in staff pages.

It receives:

- `selectedIndex`: the currently selected bottom navigation index.
- `onSelect`: callback for changing pages.
- `child`: the active page widget.

Its layout is:

```dart
Column(
  children: [
    Expanded(child: child),
    UcisBottomNav(...)
  ],
)
```

`Expanded` makes the active page take all available space above the bottom navigation.

## Staff Pages

### `StaffHomeScreen`

This is the staff dashboard.

It uses `AppScrollView`, which gives it:

- A fixed top header.
- A scrollable content area.

The header is:

- Title: `Welcome back, Dr. James Kalolo`
- Subtitle: `Staff     College of ICT`
- Leading initials: `DJ`
- Badge: `2`
- Trailing button: `J`

The content includes:

1. `_AudiencePill`
   - Shows `Lecturer     Computer Engineering and IT`.

2. `SectionCard` titled `Quick Access`
   - Contains four `QuickTile` widgets:
     - `LMS` / `Teaching`
     - `FYP` / `Review`
     - `Students` / `Manage`
     - `Grading` / `Submit`

3. `Wrap` of quick mini actions
   - `Profile`
   - `Calendar`
   - `Map`

4. `SectionCard` titled `My Tasks`
   - Contains three `TaskItem` widgets:
     - `Submit Semester I Grades`, status `Pending`, level `High`
     - `Review FYP Proposals`, status `In Progress`, level `Medium`
     - `Approve consultation slots`, status `Today`, level `Normal`

`TaskItem` colors priority badges using level:

- `High`: red.
- `Medium`: gold.
- Anything else: green.

### `AnnouncementsScreen`

This screen shows staff alerts and academic updates.

It contains:

- Header: `Announcements`
- Search field
- Horizontal filter row
- Announcement cards

Filters:

- `All`
- `Academic`
- `Events`
- `Emergency`
- `General`

Announcement examples:

- `Semester II Examination Timetable Released`
- `FYP proposal review deadline`
- `Senate results submission window`

Each announcement is rendered by `AnnouncementItem`.

### `ServicesScreen`

This screen shows staff academic systems.

It contains three `ServiceCard` widgets:

1. `ARIS`
   - Body: manage marks, class lists, course allocations, and academic records.
   - Chips: Class Lists, Marks, Courses, Reports.

2. `LMS`
   - Body: upload course materials, assignments, discussions, and online lecture resources.
   - Chips: Courses, Assignments, Resources, Forums.

3. `FYP Portal`
   - Body: review student submissions, supervisor comments, and project progress.
   - Chips: Submissions, Supervision, Review.

Each service card also shows a green `Connected` badge and an `Open ... >` button.

### `CalendarScreen`

This screen shows academic calendar items.

It uses:

- Header: `Calendar`
- `SectionCard` titled `March 2026`
- Three `EventRow` items:
  - Faculty Meeting
  - UDSM Career Fair 2026
  - Semester II Exams Start

Each event row contains:

- Calendar icon.
- Event title.
- Event metadata.
- Category badge.

### `AiAssistantScreen`

This screen shows a staff-oriented AI assistant prototype.

It contains prompt chips for common staff questions:

- How do I submit semester grades?
- Show my assigned FYP reviews.
- What classes do I teach today?
- How do I approve consultation slots?
- Where is the Health Center?
- FYP supervision guidelines?

It also contains:

- A larger empty text area for conversation output.
- A message input field.
- A disabled `Send` button.

The send button is disabled because no AI backend is connected yet.

### `CampusMapScreen`

This screen provides a campus map/search prototype.

It contains:

- Header: `Campus Map`
- Search field
- `MapPreview`
- Filter row
- Office/location list

Locations:

- College of ICT (CoICT)
- Main Library
- Health Center
- Nkrumah Hall

Each location is rendered by `LocationRow`.

## Shared Layout Widgets

### `UcisHeader`

This is the blue top header used by most screens.

Parameters:

- `title`: main title.
- `subtitle`: smaller subtitle.
- `leading`: text shown inside the left circular avatar.
- `badge`: optional red badge.
- `trailing`: optional small trailing label.
- `actions`: optional list of icons.

The header uses:

- Blue background.
- Left `CircleAvatar`.
- Title and subtitle column.
- Optional `HeaderButton` for badges/trailing labels.
- Optional `HeaderIcon` widgets.

### `AppScrollView`

This creates a consistent page structure:

```dart
Column(
  children: [
    header,
    Expanded(
      child: SingleChildScrollView(...)
    )
  ]
)
```

The header remains at the top. The page content scrolls below it. This prevents long screens from overflowing on smaller phones.

### `UcisCard`

This is the base rounded white card component.

It applies:

- White background.
- `16` padding.
- `18` corner radius.
- Light grey border.
- Soft shadow.

Most panels, lists, and cards are built from `UcisCard`.

### `SectionCard`

This is a titled card wrapper. It accepts:

- `title`
- optional `subtitle`
- `child`
- optional `trailing`

It is used for dashboard sections such as `Quick Access`, `My Tasks`, and calendar panels.

### `UdsLogo`

This renders the UDSM crest:

```dart
Image.asset('assets/images/udsm_logo.png')
```

Parameters:

- `size`: controls width.
- `compact`: when true, also forces height to the same size.

### `HeaderButton`

This renders small rounded text buttons in the header, such as:

- Notification count badges.
- Small profile labels.

If a custom color is passed, it uses that color. Otherwise, it uses semi-transparent white.

### `HeaderIcon`

This renders icon buttons used in the header, for example the back and close icons on the staff login screen.

In the current prototype these icons are visual only and do not have tap handlers.

### `_AudiencePill`

This is a small blue pill that identifies the current staff audience or role.

Current text:

```text
Lecturer     Computer Engineering and IT
```

The underscore means the widget is private to `screens.dart`.

### `QuickTile`

This renders the square quick-access items on the staff home screen.

Parameters:

- `icon`
- `title`
- `subtitle`

It uses fixed height, border, rounded corners, centered icon, title, and subtitle.

### `MiniAction`

This renders smaller shortcut cards, currently used for:

- Profile
- Calendar
- Map

It uses `UcisCard` internally and fixed width so the `Wrap` layout can place actions cleanly across the screen.

### `TaskItem`

This renders staff tasks in the dashboard.

Parameters:

- `title`
- `status`
- `level`

The `level` controls badge color:

- `High`: red.
- `Medium`: gold.
- Default: green.

This gives staff an immediate visual indication of task priority.

### `AnnouncementItem`

This renders one announcement card.

Parameters:

- `title`
- `tag`
- `level`
- `time`

It uses a `Wrap` for badges and time so the content can move to a new line instead of overflowing on narrow screens.

The body text is currently static:

```text
Official academic update for staff action, teaching coordination, and student guidance.
```

### `ServiceCard`

This renders one staff service integration.

Parameters:

- `title`
- `body`
- `chips`

It shows:

- Service icon.
- Service title.
- Green `Connected` badge.
- Description body.
- Feature chips.
- `Open ... >` button.

The button is visual for now and has an empty callback.

### `EventRow`

This renders one calendar event.

Parameters:

- `title`
- `meta`
- `tag`

It shows:

- Calendar icon.
- Event title.
- Event metadata.
- Category badge.

If the tag is `Events`, it uses gold. Otherwise, it uses blue.

### `PromptChip`

This renders a suggested AI assistant prompt.

It is an aligned rounded chip with text, white background, and border.

### `MapPreview`

This renders a placeholder campus map preview.

It uses:

- Fixed height.
- Rounded border.
- Light blue/green gradient.
- Text:
  - `UDSM Main Campus`
  - `Dar es Salaam, Tanzania`

No real map API is connected yet.

### `LocationRow`

This renders a campus location row.

Parameters:

- `title`
- `meta`

It shows:

- Pink location icon.
- Location title.
- Location metadata.
- Chevron icon.

### `FilterRow`

This renders a horizontally scrollable row of filter badges.

The first filter is shown as active blue. Other filters use pale grey styling.

The horizontal scroll prevents overflow when many filters exist.

### `BadgePill`

This is the reusable status/category badge.

Parameters:

- `text`
- `color`
- `pale`

If `pale` is false, it uses a lightly transparent version of the provided color. If `pale` is true, it uses a grey background and muted text.

This widget is reused for filters, priorities, service chips, category tags, and status indicators.

### `UcisBottomNav`

This is the signed-in Staff bottom navigation.

It receives:

- `selectedIndex`
- `onSelect`

Navigation items:

- Home
- Alerts
- Services
- Calendar
- AI
- Map

Each item calls `onSelect(i)` to change `_page`.

The selected item is blue. Unselected items are muted grey. Logout was removed from this bottom navigation and moved to the Staff Profile screen.

### Staff Profile Logout

The Staff dashboard now passes an `onOpenProfile` callback into `StaffHomeScreen`. The Profile quick action calls that callback and sets `_page` to `6`.

When `_page == 6`, the app shows `StaffProfileScreen`. This screen displays staff account details and contains the red `Logout` button. Pressing it calls the shared `_logout()` method, which resets `_page` to `-2` and returns to the welcome screen.

This keeps the staff bottom navigation focused on navigation only, while logout lives in the account/profile area.

## `lib/alumni_screens.dart`

This file contains the complete Alumni UI module. It was added as a separate file so the existing Staff UI in `screens.dart` remains readable and the Alumni UI can grow independently.

The Alumni UI is still a local Flutter prototype. It uses static mock data, local integer page IDs, and callbacks instead of real Django API calls. The UI is ready to be connected later to SSO, Django REST API endpoints, MySQL-backed data, push notifications, and the Python AI layer.

### Alumni Page Constants

At the top of `alumni_screens.dart`, each Alumni screen has a constant page number:

```dart
const alumniHomePage = 100;
const alumniUpdatesPage = 101;
const alumniEventsPage = 102;
const alumniJobsPage = 103;
const alumniProfilePage = 104;
...
const alumniAssistantPage = 132;
```

The Staff UI uses small page numbers such as `0`, `1`, `2`, and so on. Alumni pages start at `100` so they do not collide with Staff pages.

In `screens.dart`, this check decides whether the signed-in user is inside the Alumni UI:

```dart
_page >= alumniHomePage
```

If that condition is true, the app renders `AlumniShell`.

### Alumni Login Flow

`AlumniLoginScreen` is the Alumni SSO login screen. It receives three callbacks:

- `onSignIn`: opens the Alumni dashboard.
- `onRegister`: opens the Alumni registration form.
- `onBack`: returns to the shared welcome screen.

The screen includes:

- UDSM-style header.
- SSO email/student ID field.
- Password field.
- `Continue` button.
- `Register as Alumni` button.
- Security notice mentioning HTTPS/TLS, RBAC, login alerts, activity logging, and session timeout.

There is no real authentication yet. Pressing `Continue` simulates successful SSO login.

### Alumni Registration Flow

`AlumniRegistrationScreen` represents the new alumni registration request form.

It includes fields for:

- Full name.
- Student ID / matriculation number.
- Graduation year.
- Programme / department.
- Current email address.
- Current location / employer.
- Profile photo upload button.

Pressing `Submit for approval` moves to `AlumniStatusScreen.pending`.

### Registration Pending and Approved Screens

`AlumniStatusScreen` is a reusable status screen. It has two factory constructors:

- `AlumniStatusScreen.pending(...)`
- `AlumniStatusScreen.approved(...)`

Both use the same layout but show different titles, descriptions, icons, and actions.

This avoids duplicating nearly identical code for registration status pages.

### `AlumniShell`

`AlumniShell` is the main signed-in Alumni container. It receives:

- `page`: the current alumni page number.
- `onOpen`: callback for changing alumni pages.
- `onLogout`: callback for returning to the welcome screen.

It displays two main parts:

1. `Expanded(child: _body)`: the active Alumni screen.
2. `AlumniBottomNav(...)`: the Alumni five-tab bottom navigation.

The `_body` getter uses a Dart `switch` expression to map each page constant to the correct screen widget.

Examples:

```dart
alumniHomePage => AlumniDashboard(onOpen: onOpen)
alumniUpdatesPage => AlumniUpdatesScreen(onOpen: onOpen)
alumniEventsPage => AlumniEventsScreen(onOpen: onOpen)
alumniJobsPage => AlumniJobsScreen(onOpen: onOpen)
alumniProfilePage => AlumniProfileHub(onOpen: onOpen, onLogout: onLogout)
```

Detail screens are also routed here:

- Announcement detail.
- News detail.
- Event detail.
- Saved jobs.
- Alumni directory.
- Mentorship screens.
- Feedback history.
- Security notices.
- AI assistant.

### Alumni Bottom Navigation

`AlumniBottomNav` implements the required five tabs:

- Home
- Updates
- Events
- Jobs
- Profile

The selected tab is blue and the inactive tabs are muted grey.

The AI assistant is intentionally not a bottom tab. It is opened through the floating action button in `screens.dart`.

### Alumni Floating AI Button

The root `Scaffold` in `screens.dart` shows the AI floating action button only when `_page >= alumniHomePage`.

```dart
floatingActionButton: _page >= alumniHomePage && _page != alumniAssistantPage
```

The button opens `alumniAssistantPage`.

It is wrapped in:

```dart
Padding(
  padding: const EdgeInsets.only(bottom: 72),
  child: FloatingActionButton(...)
)
```

This raises the chatbot button above the Alumni bottom navigation so it does not cover the Profile tab.

### Alumni Dashboard

`AlumniDashboard` is the Alumni home screen. It uses `RefreshIndicator` so pull-to-refresh exists in the UI prototype.

It includes:

- Personalized welcome header.
- Policy update notice.
- Latest announcements card.
- Administration and DARUSO announcements shown with distinct tags/colors.
- Upcoming events shortcut.
- Job highlights shortcut.
- Mentorship shortcut.
- Latest news shortcut.
- Emergency shortcut.
- AI Assistant shortcut.
- Campus map shortcut.
- Cached content/offline shortcut.

All dashboard cards call `onOpen(pageNumber)` to navigate to the correct Alumni screen.

### Updates, Announcements, and News

`AlumniUpdatesScreen` combines announcements and news.

It includes:

- Search field.
- Filter chips.
- Administration announcements section.
- DARUSO announcements section.
- News feed section.

Administration and DARUSO content are separated to satisfy the requirement that those streams remain visually distinct.

`AlumniDetailScreen.announcement(...)` shows the announcement detail page. It includes:

- Full title.
- Posted-by/date subtitle.
- Category badge.
- Mock image/attachment area.
- Body text.
- Download attachment button.

`AlumniDetailScreen.news(...)` shows the news article detail page with body text and share action.

### Events and Almanac

`AlumniEventsScreen` is a `StatefulWidget` because it stores whether the user is viewing events as a list or as a calendar.

The local boolean is:

```dart
bool calendar = false;
```

`SegmentedButton<bool>` toggles between:

- List view.
- Calendar view.

The screen includes:

- Event category filters.
- Alumni-specific highlighted events.
- `My Events` button.
- `Almanac` button.

`AlumniDetailScreen.event(...)` shows event details with:

- Date/time/location.
- Description.
- RSVP / Subscribe button.
- Ask AI button.

`AlumniListScreen.subscribed(...)` shows subscribed events and reminders.

`AlumniListScreen.almanac(...)` shows a read-only academic calendar list.

### Job Board

`AlumniJobsScreen` implements the Alumni job board.

It includes:

- Job search field.
- Industry/location/job-type filters.
- Job cards with title, employer, location, and deadline.
- Saved jobs button.

`AlumniJobDetailScreen` shows:

- Full job description.
- Employer.
- Location.
- Deadline.
- Apply / Visit link button.
- Save job button.

Jobs are shown as admin-posted content. Alumni can browse, save, and apply, but not create jobs.

### Profile, Directory, and Networking

`AlumniProfileHub` is the main Alumni profile tab.

It includes:

- Public profile shortcut.
- Edit profile shortcut.
- Notification preferences shortcut.
- Policy notice shortcut.
- Alumni directory.
- Networking hub.
- Mentorship.
- Student organizations.
- Feedback submission.
- Login alert screen.
- Suspicious activity screen.
- Logout button.

`AlumniPublicProfileScreen` shows the logged-in alumnus public-facing card with name, programme, year, current role, and bio.

`AlumniEditProfileScreen` contains editable fields for:

- Name.
- Bio.
- Current job title.
- Employer.
- Location.
- Contact email.
- LinkedIn profile.
- Account status.

`AlumniDirectoryScreen` provides search and filters for finding other alumni.

`OtherAlumniProfileScreen` shows another alumnus profile with `Connect` and `Message` buttons.

`AlumniNetworkingScreen` shows:

- Pending/accepted connections.
- Groups/communities.
- A basic message thread.

### Mentorship and Campus Life

`AlumniMentorshipScreen` covers Alumni mentorship participation.

It includes:

- Become a mentor shortcut.
- Mentorship connections shortcut.
- Student mentorship request row.
- Browse mentors row.

`AlumniMentorFormScreen` contains:

- Mentorship category chips.
- Expertise field.
- Availability field.
- Mentor profile summary.
- Submit mentor profile button.

`AlumniMentorshipRequestScreen` shows a mock student request with Accept and Decline actions.

`AlumniOrganizationsScreen` lists student organizations, categories, contact leads, and historical links such as "Former member".

### Emergency Contacts

`AlumniEmergencyScreen` shows view-only emergency contacts:

- Campus Security.
- Medical Centre.
- Fire & Rescue.
- Alumni Office.

Each row is represented by `EmergencyContact`, which displays the contact role, phone number, availability, and a "Quick-call" tag.

The `Get help from AI` button opens the Alumni AI assistant with emergency context implied by the screen.

### Campus Map

`AlumniMapScreen` provides a prototype campus map.

It includes:

- Search field.
- Category filters.
- Map preview area.
- Location pins for Library, CoICT, and Health.
- Get directions button.
- Ask AI button.

The current map is static UI. Later it can be connected to the UDSM Campus Map API.

### AI Assistant

`AlumniAssistantScreen` is the Alumni chatbot interface.

It includes:

- Header.
- Intro bot message.
- Suggested quick query chips:
  - Find a location.
  - Show upcoming events.
  - Emergency contacts.
  - Latest announcements.
- Text input.
- Send button.

The screen is UI-only for now. Later it can connect to the Python AI layer.

### Feedback

`AlumniFeedbackScreen` includes:

- Feedback type selector chips.
- Message text area.
- Screenshot attachment button.
- Anonymous submission toggle.
- Submit feedback button.

After submission, the app opens `AlumniFeedbackConfirmationScreen`.

`AlumniListScreen.feedback(...)` shows feedback history and response status.

### Notification Preferences

`AlumniPreferencesScreen` shows toggle rows for:

- Announcements.
- Events.
- Jobs.
- Mentorship requests.
- News.
- Alumni event notifications.

These are static toggles in the prototype. Later they can write to a backend notification preference endpoint.

### Security, Policy, and Offline Notices

`AlumniNoticeScreen` is a reusable notice screen with factory constructors:

- `loginAlert(...)`
- `suspicious(...)`
- `policy(...)`
- `offline(...)`

This keeps login alerts, suspicious activity warnings, policy notices, and offline/cached-content notices consistent.

### Shared Alumni Helper Widgets

The Alumni module defines several reusable UI widgets:

- `AlumniScroll`: common header + scrollable body layout.
- `AlumniHeader`: blue UDSM header with initials, title, subtitle, optional badge, and optional back button.
- `UcisPanel`: white card container.
- `SectionBlock`: titled card section.
- `DashboardTile`: tappable dashboard card.
- `CompactFeedItem`: reusable announcement/news/event/job row.
- `JobPost`: job-specific wrapper around `CompactFeedItem`.
- `FilterChips`: horizontal category filter row.
- `BadgePill`: small rounded category/status badge.
- `ActionPill`: compact shortcut chip.
- `MenuAction`: profile menu row.
- `NoticeLine`: yellow notice banner.
- `CalendarPreview`: mock month grid.
- `EmergencyContact`: emergency row.
- `MapPin`: map marker widget.
- `AlumniPerson`: alumni directory row.
- `ConnectionRow`: networking/mentorship connection row.
- `ChatBubble`: AI assistant message bubble.

These helpers reduce repetition and make the Alumni UI easier to extend.

### How Alumni Navigation Works

The Alumni UI does not use Flutter named routes yet. It uses simple integer page constants and callbacks.

For example:

```dart
ActionPill(
  icon: Icons.map_outlined,
  label: 'Campus map',
  onTap: () => onOpen(alumniMapPage),
)
```

When the user taps the chip:

1. The callback sends `alumniMapPage` to `AlumniShell`.
2. `screens.dart` stores that value in `_page`.
3. Flutter rebuilds.
4. `AlumniShell._body` sees `alumniMapPage`.
5. The app displays `AlumniMapScreen`.

This is simple and works well for a prototype. A production version can later migrate to named routes, `go_router`, or Navigator 2.0.

## `test/widget_test.dart`

The widget test verifies both the Staff and Alumni entry flows.

Test name:

```text
staff and alumni can sign in from the shared welcome screen
```

The test performs these steps:

1. Renders `UcisAdminApp`.
2. Confirms the welcome screen exists.
3. Confirms `Login as Staff`, `Login as Alumni`, and `Login as Student` are visible.
4. Taps `Login as Staff`.
5. Confirms `Staff Login` appears.
6. Taps `Continue`.
7. Confirms the staff dashboard appears by checking:
   - `Dr. James Kalolo`
   - `Quick Access`
   - `My Tasks`
8. Taps `Profile`.
9. Confirms `Staff account details` appears.
10. Taps `Logout`.
11. Confirms the app returns to `Login as Staff`.
12. Taps `Login as Alumni`.
13. Confirms `Alumni Login` and `Register as Alumni` appear.
14. Taps `Continue`.
15. Confirms the Alumni session timeout warning appears.
16. Dismisses the warning.
17. Confirms the Alumni dashboard appears by checking:
    - `Welcome home`
    - `Latest announcements`

This test protects the shared role entry screen, Staff login/dashboard/profile logout flow, and Alumni login/dashboard/session-warning flow from accidental breakage.

## Important Current Limitations

This is still a UI prototype. The following parts are not connected to real services yet:

- Staff authentication.
- Alumni SSO authentication.
- Alumni registration approval backend.
- Student/Admin role flows.
- ARIS/LMS/FYP links.
- AI assistant backend.
- Campus map API.
- Real notification data.
- Real calendar data.
- Real staff task data.
- Real alumni directory, jobs, mentorship, and feedback data.
- Push notification deep-link handling.
- Real automatic session timeout enforcement.

The current implementation uses static UI data so the screens can be demonstrated and reviewed before backend integration.

## Verification

The current implementation was verified with:

```sh
flutter analyze
flutter test
```

Both commands pass.
